.TH "YAMLR-UPGRADE" "1" "November 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
\fBRelease Upgrade & Offline Token Management\fR
.PP
The \fByamlr upgrade\fR command displays offline release upgrade instructions and guides teams on updating the native binary and offline license entitlements.
.PP
> [!NOTE]
.PP
> \fBKubernetes API Migrations:\fR To modernize deprecated Kubernetes API versions (e.g., \fBextensions/v1beta1\fR -> \fBapps/v1\fR, Ingress migrations), use the dedicated [\fByamlr migrate\fR](yamlr_migrate.md) command.
.PP
.SH "USAGE"
.nf
.RS
# Display upgrade instructions and release check
yamlr upgrade

# Check active license and upgrade options
yamlr subscribe
.RE
.fi
.SH "OPTIONS & FLAGS"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB-h, --help\fR: Display help information.
.SH "UPGRADING THE STANDALONE BINARY"
Yamlr is distributed as a single standalone native binary. To upgrade:
.PP
.SS "Homebrew (macOS & Linux)"
.nf
.RS
brew update && brew upgrade yamlr/tap/yamlr
.RE
.fi
.SS "GitHub Releases (Direct Download)"
Download the latest pre-compiled archive for your architecture:
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Linux x86_64: \fByamlr-linux-x86_64.tar.gz\fR
.IP "\(bu" 2
Linux aarch64: \fByamlr-linux-aarch64.tar.gz\fR
.IP "\(bu" 2
macOS Apple Silicon: \fByamlr-macos-aarch64.tar.gz\fR
.IP "\(bu" 2
macOS Intel: \fByamlr-macos-x86_64.tar.gz\fR
.IP "\(bu" 2
Windows x64: \fByamlr-windows-x86_64.zip\fR
Extract and overwrite your existing \fByamlr\fR binary. No system dependencies or runtime packages are required.
.PP
.SH "RELATED COMMANDS"
.IP "\(bu" 2
[\fByamlr migrate\fR](yamlr_migrate.md) — Modernize deprecated Kubernetes API versions.
.IP "\(bu" 2
[\fByamlr auth\fR](yamlr_auth.md) — Inspect or activate air-gapped signed license tokens.
.IP "\(bu" 2
[\fByamlr version\fR](yamlr_version.md) — Show current binary version and architecture.
